  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nFrom https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#tables-2:\n\n```css\ncolgroup[hidden], col[hidden], thead[hidden], tbody[hidden],\ntfoot[hidden], tr[hidden] {\n  visibility: collapse;\n}\n```\n\nFrom https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#hidden-elements:\n```css\n[hidden]:not([hidden=until-found i]):not(embed) {\n  display: none;\n}\n```\n\nThe specificity of this last rule overrides the first. This means that the table parts that are hidden are assigned `display: none`. Note that at least Gecko and Blink treat `hidden` as presentation attribute, but all browsers seem to fail a test that verifies this behavior: https://wpt.fyi/results/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/tables/hidden-attr.html?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=%2Fhtml%2Frendering%2Fnon-replaced-elements%2Ftables%2Fhidden-attr.html",
